    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_Title">Online artwork</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_TmdbConfigHelp">When a token is configured, TMDB is preferred for movies, TV shows and anime. Add your TMDB API Read Access Token below to enable localized artwork.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_TmdbConfigTitle">TMDB ARTWORK — MOVIES &amp; SERIES</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_EnableHelp">Local artwork always has priority. With a TMDB token, movies and TV shows try TMDB first; TVMaze and AniList remain automatic keyless alternatives.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_Enable">Enable online artwork</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_Desc">Automatically retrieve artwork when no local image is available. Aniki selects the appropriate provider automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_MoviesTitle">MOVIES — TMDB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_SeriesTitle">TV SERIES — TMDB / TVMAZE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_AnimeTitle">ANIME — TMDB / ANILIST</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTvmaze_Enable">Enable TVmaze series scraper</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTvmaze_Help">No API key is required. TVmaze is used as the fallback for TV series when TMDB is unavailable or cannot find a safe match.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoAnilist_Enable">Enable AniList anime scraper</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoAnilist_Help">No API key is required. AniList is the specialized anime fallback when TMDB is unavailable or cannot find a safe match, and remains available in the artwork picker.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_AutoRoutingHelp">Automatic routing with a TMDB token: movie → TMDB; TV series → TMDB then TVMaze; anime → TMDB then AniList/TVMaze. Without a token, TVMaze and AniList remain available automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoOnlineArtwork_Attribution">The TMDB token is optional for series and anime: it enables TMDB as the preferred provider. TVMaze and AniList remain available without a key.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTvmaze_StatusReady">TVmaze scraper: Ready</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTvmaze_StatusDisabled">TVmaze scraper: Disabled</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoAnilist_StatusReady">AniList scraper: Ready</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoAnilist_StatusDisabled">AniList scraper: Disabled</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_Title">TMDB artwork scraper</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_Desc">Automatically retrieve Cover, Landscape, Wallpaper and Logo artwork from TMDB for movies, TV shows and anime when local artwork is unavailable.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_Enable">Enable TMDB artwork scraper</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_EnableHelp">Local artwork placed next to the media always has priority. TMDB is used only when local artwork is unavailable.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_Language">Preferred artwork language</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_LanguageAuto">Use Playnite language</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_LanguageHelp">Artwork with text prefers this language, then textless artwork, the media original language and English. Wallpapers prefer textless artwork.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_Token">TMDB API Read Access Token</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_TokenHelp">Create a free developer API Read Access Token in your TMDB account settings. The token is stored locally encrypted with Windows DPAPI.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_MatchingHelp">V2 cleans release names (quality, codec, language, source and release-group tags), extracts the year separately, tries smart title variants and scores title/year matches before accepting them.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_PrivacyHelp">When scraping is needed, Aniki sends only the cleaned media title and detected year to TMDB. Local/network paths are never sent to TMDB or stored in clear text in the artwork indexes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_Attribution">This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_StatusDisabled">TMDB scraper: Disabled</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_StatusTokenMissing">TMDB scraper: API token missing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VideoTmdb_StatusReady">TMDB scraper: Ready</sys:String>

